# GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark - self-exclusion (no verified public benchmarks)

- Source: OpenAI (`gpt-5.3-codex-spark`)
- Date: 2026-10-05 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Negative findings - why this file is `.md.excluded`

As of 2026-10-05, no verified public benchmark scores exist for `gpt-5.3-codex-spark`:

- OpenAI's Feb 12, 2026 launch post says it is stronger than GPT-5.1-Codex-mini on SWE-Bench Pro and Terminal-Bench 2.0, but publishes no numbers.
- The Cerebras co-launch blog makes the same qualitative claim without a table.
- BenchLM / Artificial Analysis / vals.ai carry zero sourced benchmark rows for the exact ID.
- CloudPrice lists spec (128K context, text in/text out, image input in one listing) but no pricing or benchmark row.

Writing normalized scores would require inventing rows; re-research after OpenAI or a third party publishes per-benchmark numbers.
